<title>UK: Toad appoints CEO, fixes window product pact.</title>
<headline>Toad appoints CEO, fixes window product pact.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>British consumer products company Toad Plc said on Monday that it appointed Charles Parker as group chief executive effective January 1997.</p>
<p>Parker is moving from industrial group Charter Plc where he was commercial director, and will leave on December 31. Separately, Toad said that it had concluded negotiations with the UK unit of Mercedes Benz to market Toad's vehicle window security product to its customers. At 1150 GMT Toad shares were marked up at 89.50 pence from Friday's close of 87.50 pence.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
